## AIM

- The purpose of this Qualification Standard (QS) is to describe in operational terms, the required outcome of individual training and education (IT&E) for Cyber Operators (CYBER OP) employed in the Job of Senior Cyber Defence Analyst (Sr Cyber Def Analyst).

## OUTLINE OF TRAINING

			- Commanders require personnel who possess the knowledge and skills necessary to perform the many tasks required of a CYBER OP employed as a Sr Cyber Def Analyst. This job is performed in support of the Sea, Land, Air and CANSOF elements. The primary responsibility is to lead a cyber team in fulfilling technical tasks of applying advanced defensive cyber operations techniques, such as threat hunting through statistical analysis.

- The loading authority must ensure that candidates meet those prerequisites. 

## BACKGROUND

- This document contains the following Performance Objectives (POs) that the member shall achieve to meet the requirements of this qualification:

| **PO** | **PO Title** |
| --- | --- |
| 001 | Build Cyber Operation Software Tools |
| 002 | Analyze Windows Enterprise Networks |
| 003 | Conduct Cyber Threat Emulation |
| 004 | Analyze Malware |
| 005 | Analyze Digital Artifacts |
| 006 | Conduct Advanced Analysis and Exploitation |
| 007 | Analyze Non-IT Systems |
| 008 | Defend a Network Under Attack |

## USE OF QUALIFICATION STANDARD

- This QS shall be used by the IT&E establishment to design, develop, conduct, and evaluate the training program.

- This QS will also be used by MPGTG Standards in support of validation.

- The qualification code/title supported by the POs:

| **Qualification Code** | **National Qualification Title** |
| --- | --- |
| Temp 67 | Rank Qualification Cyber Operator Corporal |

	

