| 21 | Board reviewed PO 001. 1.d.2 intended to be at the level to use and troubleshoot automated machine learning tools such as elastic machine learning. 1.d.3 intended to have the cyber operator use cryptographic primitives such as block ciphers, hashes, asymmetric algorithms to implement high level cryptographic systems. | Nil |
| 22 | Discussing verbiage to properly capture what expectation we have of a DP2 candidate – “Implement a TLS/SSH key exchange and encryption system using a cryptographic library” Task: Implement mathematics for cryptography and statistical analysis. | Nil |
| 23 | Board reviewed and discussed given para. No change required, consensus across the board that they are accurate | Nil |
| 24 | Board discussion involved all 8 POs and the current issues with the training. Discussed the fact that we are not going to be able to fix the cyber operator trade. We are building the DPs to help the future of the trade, not working on solving the current issues that exist in the trade. The focus should be on what we want our Cpl/MCpl to do. | D Cyber FD for consideration |
| 25 | Discussion around integration with other agencies and the way forward for more integration spaces, possibilities to gain OJE experience by working with other GoC departments. | D Cyber FD for consideration |
