| 36 | Board agrees that PO 004 has been updated and tasks are properly justified and assigned. | Nil |
| 37 | Maj Carter speaks to the board, structure of Cyber Op trade and reserve career path. Expanded on career path and specialization. Using USQ/OSQ in order to enhance your knowledge of a particular topic. Issues with retention and how to possibly help keep people in. What can we do? What would help retain people? We have the opportunity to structure the occupation into a flexible manner. Better management and communication. Work the DP boards with a bit of assumption to setup the Cpl/MCpl RQ in a way to have realistic expectations of the tasks that need completion Discussed Willis College program, STEP and new contract, what our expectation is of the students coming onto DP1.2 from DP1.1 Introduced HackerRank Assessment Tool; discussed possibilities to build evaluations in it to confirm training. Certification vs Assessment; Why is it important and are we able to lean on that in order to prove effectiveness of the member. Board feels it’s important to pay for certifications. | Nil |
| 38 | **PO 005** Reviewed and updated task Numbers; New – conduct digital media duplication New – conduct live artifact acquisition New – identify operating systems based on network traffic New – Produce an activity timeline New – conduct OS forensics New – Conduct live memory acquisition The six above are new tasks for PO 005. | As per Ser #3 |
| 39 | Board discussed changes made to PO 005 and came to an agreement that it is good to go, all changes approved. | Nil |
